As I understand it it&#x27;s basically how Pytorch works. A clever trick but also super confusing because while it <i>seems</i> like normal code, as soon as you try and do something that you could totally do in normal code it doesn&#x27;t work:<p><pre><code>  let friendsWithPhotos = friendsPromise.map(friend =&gt; {
    return {friend, photo: friend.has_photo ? api.getUserPhoto(friend.id) : default_photo};
  }
</code></pre>
Looks totally reasonable, but it&#x27;s not going to work properly. You might not even realise until it&#x27;s deployed.
